Project-Planning
: Project Initiation & Requirement Analysis
Duration: Week 1
•	Identify the problem: students need personalized, interactive, and easily accessible academic assistance.
•	Define the objective of EduGenie, an AI-powered learning assistant using Google Gemini.
•	Identify target users: students, teachers, and administrators.
•	Collect functional and non-functional requirements.
•	Define project scope, limitations, and expected outcomes.
•	Study existing AI learning assistants and identify gaps.
Deliverables:
•	Problem Statement
•	Objectives
•	Scope of the Project
•	Requirement Specification
•	Initial Project Proposal
________________________________________
Phase 2: System Analysis & Technology Selection
Duration: Week 2
•	Analyze the requirements and determine the system architecture.
•	Select technologies for frontend, backend, database, and AI integration.
•	Study the Google Gemini API and its capabilities for educational applications.
•	Define how user queries will be processed and how AI-generated responses will be delivered.
•	Identify security, privacy, and authentication requirements.
Possible Technologies:
•	Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript / React
•	Backend: Python Flask / FastAPI or Node.js
•	AI: Google Gemini API
•	Database: MySQL / MongoDB / Firebase
•	Authentication: Firebase Authentication or JWT
Deliverables:
•	Technology Stack
•	Feasibility Analysis
•	System Requirements
•	Initial Architecture
________________________________________
Phase 3: System Design
Duration: Weeks 3–4
•	Design the overall architecture of EduGenie.
•	Design user roles and access permissions.
•	Create database structure and relationships.
•	Design user interface screens.
•	Define the communication flow between the application, backend, database, and Gemini API.
•	Prepare UML diagrams.
Major Modules:
1.	User Registration & Login
2.	Student Dashboard
3.	AI Chat Assistant
4.	Question & Answer Module
5.	Study Material Assistance
6.	Quiz/Assessment Module
7.	Personalized Learning Module
8.	Progress Tracking
9.	Admin Module
Deliverables:
•	System Architecture Diagram
•	Use Case Diagram
•	Class Diagram
•	Activity/Sequence Diagrams
•	ER Diagram
•	UI Wireframes
________________________________________
Phase 4: Database & Backend Development
Duration: Weeks 5–6
•	Create the database and required collections/tables.
•	Implement user authentication.
•	Develop APIs for users, learning content, quizzes, and progress.
•	Implement data validation and error handling.
•	Establish secure communication between frontend and backend.
•	Create the service layer for Gemini API integration.
Deliverables:
•	Working Database
•	Backend APIs
•	Authentication System
•	API Documentation
________________________________________
Phase 5: Google Gemini AI Integration
Duration: Weeks 7–8
•	Integrate Google Gemini into the application.
•	Develop the AI chat interface.
•	Create prompts designed specifically for educational assistance.
•	Implement contextual question answering.
•	Add features such as:
o	Topic explanations
o	Summaries
o	Question generation
o	Quiz generation
o	Step-by-step problem solving
o	Study-plan suggestions
•	Implement safeguards for inappropriate, irrelevant, or unreliable responses.
•	Test response quality and latency.
Deliverables:
•	Functional Gemini Integration
•	AI Prompt Design
•	AI Learning Assistant Module
•	Response Validation Mechanism
________________________________________
Phase 6: Frontend Development
Duration: Weeks 9–10
•	Develop the student dashboard.
•	Build the AI chat interface.
•	Implement learning-material and quiz interfaces.
•	Display learning progress through charts/cards.
•	Add responsive design for desktop and mobile devices.
•	Connect frontend components with backend APIs.
Deliverables:
•	Complete User Interface
•	Responsive Web Application
•	Integrated Frontend + Backend
________________________________________
Phase 7: Personalized Learning & Assessment
Duration: Week 11
•	Track user learning activities.
•	Analyze quiz performance and completed topics.
•	Generate personalized learning recommendations.
•	Provide quizzes based on selected subjects/topics.
•	Store scores and learning history.
•	Display progress reports.
Deliverables:
•	Personalized Learning Module
•	Quiz System
•	Progress Tracking
•	Student Performance Report
________________________________________
Phase 8: Testing & Validation
Duration: Week 12
Conduct different levels of testing:
•	Unit Testing: Test individual modules.
•	Integration Testing: Test communication between frontend, backend, database, and Gemini.
•	System Testing: Test the complete application.
•	UI Testing: Verify usability and responsiveness.
•	Performance Testing: Check response time and system performance.
•	Security Testing: Test authentication and data protection.
•	AI Response Testing: Evaluate accuracy, relevance, consistency, and educational usefulness.
Deliverables:
•	Test Cases
•	Test Results
•	Bug Reports
•	Corrected Application
________________________________________
Phase 9: Deployment & Documentation
Duration: Week 13
•	Deploy the application to a suitable hosting platform.
•	Configure production environment variables and API credentials securely.
•	Perform final system verification.
•	Prepare technical documentation.
•	Prepare user manual and installation/setup instructions.
Deliverables:
•	Deployed EduGenie Application
•	User Manual
•	Technical Documentation
•	Installation Guide
________________________________________
Phase 10: Evaluation & Final Presentation
Duration: Week 14
•	Demonstrate all major functionalities.
•	Evaluate the system against the original objectives.
•	Collect feedback from sample users.
•	Analyze project results.
•	Document limitations and possible future enhancements.
•	Prepare final project report and presentation.
Deliverables:
•	Final Project Report
•	Presentation/PPT
•	Demonstration
•	Evaluation Results
•	Future Enhancement Plan
Overall Project Timeline
Phase	Activity	Duration
1	Initiation & Requirement Analysis	Week 1
2	System Analysis & Technology Selection	Week 2
3	System Design	Weeks 3–4
4	Database & Backend Development	Weeks 5–6
5	Gemini AI Integration	Weeks 7–8
6	Frontend Development	Weeks 9–10
7	Personalization & Assessment	Week 11
8	Testing & Validation	Week 12
9	Deployment & Documentation	Week 13
10	Evaluation & Final Presentation	Week 14

